{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>Before she travailed.</b> From the root חיל like כיולדה (Psalms 48:7). The meaning: the children of Zion shall come without toil, like a woman who gives birth to children without toil." "<b>And brought forth.</b> Same meaning as ילדה. Similarly: שמה קננה קפוד ותמלט (Isaiah 34:15). And if they are two binyanim, the meaning is: the children of Zion shall come without toil from the four winds suddenly, as though she travailed and gave birth to children in a single day — and it is a wondrous thing."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 66, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:01:11.064006708Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}